Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a structural collapse at our client's Woodruff Road complex. Our reference is RK/MFG/2024/2210. This is reported within the 48-hour requirement for an occurrence reasonably expected to exceed half the deductible - it comfortably will.

Policy number: CP-2210-55870
Insured name: Fairmount Textile Mills Holdings, Inc.
Claimant: Fairmount Technical Fabrics, Inc.
Date of loss: 14 May 2025
Loss location: 1180 Woodruff Industrial Road, Greenville, SC 29607
Cause: Collapse - bolted connection failure on a storage mezzanine
Estimated loss: USD 8,700,000

A steel storage mezzanine in Building 1D gave way during a routine let-down of
fabric rolls. About 1,740 sq ft of deck came down onto the racking and the
pick-and-pack area below. Nobody was on it and nobody was struck.

The collapse sheared two ESFR branch lines. The system was isolated at 15:52 and a
fire watch has run continuously since 16:05; the city has been notified. We are
giving you formal notice of the impairment now, within the 24 hours the warranty
requires for an impairment exceeding eight hours.

I should flag two coverage questions rather than let them arrive later: the defect
exclusion and its write-back for resulting damage, and whether overloading beyond
the posted placard is an excluded cause on this form. The engineer's report
addresses both on the facts.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * structural engineer's report
  * loss schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster today. We would also like your
view on whether you or we should issue preservation correspondence to Foothills
Material Handling Systems, who designed and installed the mezzanine in 2018.

Kind regards,

